---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "Kief"
letter: "K"
anchor: "kief"
category: "edibles"
---

The collected trichomes that have separated from cannabis flower — the fine, powdery, crystalline material that accumulates in the bottom chamber of a grinder. Kief is significantly more potent than flower because it's a concentrated collection of trichomes, which are where cannabinoids and terpenes are produced. Can be used in infusions (using less material than flower for equivalent potency), pressed into hash, or added directly to food after decarboxylation.

→ [How to Make Cannabutter](/edibles/cannabis-infused-butter-cannabutter/), [How to Decarb Cannabis](/edibles/decarb-activate-cannabis-edibles/)
